    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d488-a2">

                <pb facs="1314" n="1308" sameAs="frus:frus1894app2/pg1308"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure No. 2.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Willis to Mr. Dole.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Honolulu, Hawaiian Islands</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1894-02-14"><hi rendition="#italic">February
                                14, 1894</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your communication of this date in further answer to my letter of the 19th
                    ultimo, and to inform you that on the 20th ultimo I was notified by my
                    Government that the Hawaiian question had been submitted to Congress and that my
                    special instructions had been fully complied with. Copies of all the letters
                    embraced in the correspondence have been transmitted to Washington.</p>
                <p>With assurance of high esteem, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Albert S. Willis.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
